{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310544,"nonce":"aCkCui1ENpbQ3W/2v0iZfw/Ght0=","title":"mark_as_extern leaves bodyless stubs in module.functions, so any fixpoint seeded from that map reads them as proven-safe","message":"`mark_as_extern` (mir_builder.rs) CLEARS `func.cfg.blocks` but LEAVES the entry\nin `module.functions`. `compilation.rs` says it outright: \"externs are in the\nfunctions map with empty CFGs\".\n\nAny interprocedural fixpoint seeded from `module.functions` therefore gives\nevery runtime stub an optimistic bottom value it can never escalate -- there is\nno body for the analysis to find evidence in -- and a later `map.get(fid)`\nreads that present-but-empty entry as PROVEN SAFE. The pessimistic\n`None =\u003e unknown` default only ever fires for a callee absent from the map\nentirely, and bodyless-but-present is the COMMON case.\n\n**Fixed 57f97b54** in `compiler/src/ir/insert_free.rs` via a `bodied(module)`\nhelper that filters `blocks.is_empty()`, so a missing entry means unknown.\n`insert_free_for_function` already had that guard for itself; the maps did not.\n\nSame shape, same file, same commit: `classify_func` matched libc names BARE\nagainst local functions as well as externs. Haxe method names lower bare, so a\nuser's `Pool.malloc(n:Int):Int` was classified as the allocator and the dest of\nevery call registered as a heap allocation -- `p.malloc(21)` returns 42 and the\nrelease was `free((void*)42)`, SIGABRT at teardown after the program's own\noutput. Only a DECLARATION is the intrinsic.\n\n**Suspect this pattern anywhere else a pass folds over `module.functions`.**\n`compute_param_retention` has the identical structure and is still gated behind\n`RZT_PARAM_RETENTION`; check it before ungating.\n\nRelated: [[feedback-fqn-first-resolution]] (bare-name lookup IS the defect) and\n[[bugs-xmodule-resolution-disease-cluster]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_bodyless_externs_answer_interprocedural_queries` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}